"epic actions element" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-actions&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-actions&gt; element: a block's actions row on an epic page, its buttons over the block's top right corner.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph><text code>&lt;epic-actions&gt;</> is a block's actions row on an epic page: the one row of a paragraph's, a list's or a table's own controls, a line of no height just before the block, its buttons over the block's top right corner. The comments' bullhorn comes first, then a table's expand button.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone adding a control to a block, or changing where the bullhorns sit.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> P45), its own <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-actions" link="/epic/src/components/epic-actions/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-actions/" code>epic-actions</></> family.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-actions-epicactions-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-actions/EpicActions.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-actions/EpicActions.en.ts" code>EpicActions.en.ts</></></>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-actions-epicactions-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-actions/EpicActions.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-actions/EpicActions.tsx" code>EpicActions.tsx</></>.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>A row with two buttons, before a paragraph, as the docs runtime makes it.</>
		<example "Example">
			<html>
				<ui-stack style="position: relative; padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed var(--ui-border-color)">
					<epic-actions style="--spell-block-gap: 0px">
						<ui-button appearance="basic circular" size="mini" icon="bullhorn" aria-label="Comment"></ui-button>
						<ui-button appearance="basic" size="mini" icon="arrows left right" aria-label="Expand"></ui-button>
					</epic-actions>
					<ui-text style="margin: 0" paragraph>A paragraph of an epic page: its controls sit over its top right corner, on the page's ground, and never push its text aside.</ui-text>
				</ui-stack>
			</html>
		</example>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Nobody writes it in a page: the docs runtime makes it the first time a block gets a control (<link target="src-spell-epic-src-tools-assets-spell-doc-helpers-js" link="/epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-helpers.js"><text title="epic/src/tools/_assets/spell-doc-helpers.js" code>addBlockAction()</></>), and takes it away with its last.</>
			<item>On every page: every page that draws one loads the epics pack (the docs runtime, the component sets' layouts).</>
			<item><text code>data-spell-added</>: a live update steps around it.</>
			<item>Where the block's top edge lies is the runtime's to measure (the block's own top margin may lie between them): it hands it in as <text code>--spell-block-gap</>, and for a table <text code>--spell-block-head</> and <text code>head-row</>.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Attributes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="table columns"/>
		<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
			<row header>
				<cell>Name</>
				<cell>What it is</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>head-row</>
				</>
				<cell>Its block is a table: the buttons centred on its header row.</>
			</>
			<row>
				<cell>
					<text code>::part(base)</>
				</>
				<cell>The controls' box, out of the flow, over the block's corner.</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>2px inside the block's top and right edges (<text code>--epic-actions-inset</>), 2px between the buttons (<text code>--epic-actions-gap</>).</>
			<item>Each button round, on the page's ground (<text code>--epic-actions-background</>).</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-10-25 against branch <ui-text code>epic-engine</> (P45).</>
		</>
	</>
